// 5.63: a coupled element may now declare a rheology, but not a valve (5.18).
// (n, K, tau_0) are forwarded to the 3D partner region's per-face viscosity;
// the transient row clears its own wall-law fields and still charges only R*q,
// so the wall is never billed twice. The checker asserts that the transient
// trace is bit-identical to a twin case with the three keys removed.
// The name keeps `reject` only for historical continuity with the earlier refusal.
// verified by tests/check_transient_power_law.py (family 9, third member lifted).
fluid { rho 850; mu 0.1; }
nodes { A { fixedPressure 3.0e4; } B { fixedPressure 2.0e4; } }
pipes { Bad { from A; to B; length 20; diameter 0.02;
              coupledResistance 5.0e8; flowIndex 0.6; consistency 1.0; } }
time  { dt 0.02; endTime 0.1; reportEvery 1; }
